WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.715 --> 00:00:09.436
David Barron: Hey! Can you hear me? I'm recording this, by the way, just so I don't lose the details. Is that okay?

2
00:00:14.982 --> 00:00:23.027
Niamh Barron: Ha, yes, that's fine, honestly that's smart. Half the family's going to ask me the same five questions. Can you hear me alright?

3
00:00:23.347 --> 00:00:25.921
Niamh Barron: I'm on the laptop in the kitchen.

4
00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:33.403
David Barron: Yeah, you're great. Little bit of echo but fine. How's everything going? It's, what, six o'clock there?

5
00:00:34.491 --> 00:00:41.894
Niamh Barron: Just after six, yeah. It's going. The list of things to do is getting shorter, which is the main thing.

6
00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:49.458
David Barron: Okay, so, logistics. I wrote down a few questions. First one: it's definitely Saturday the eleventh of July?

7
00:00:50.366 --> 00:00:59.611
Niamh Barron: Saturday the eleventh, yes. Ceremony at two o'clock at the church, then coaches out to the reception venue. It's about forty minutes out of the city.

8
00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.497
David Barron: Okay. And the coaches leave from where?

9
00:01:04.543 --> 00:01:13.021
Niamh Barron: From outside the church, around half four, after photos. And they'll bring people back to the hotel at the end of the night.

10
00:01:13.149 --> 00:01:18.161
Niamh Barron: There's a late one at half twelve and a last one at half one.

11
00:01:18.809 --> 00:01:24.778
David Barron: Perfect, that's exactly what I wanted to know. So I don't need a car at all.

12
00:01:25.911 --> 00:01:30.058
Niamh Barron: You definitely don't need a car. Please don't rent a car.

13
00:01:31.206 --> 00:01:40.568
David Barron: Ha, okay. No car. Second thing, the hotel block. You sent the group code in the email, but I wasn't sure if the rate covers breakfast.

14
00:01:41.609 --> 00:01:49.589
Niamh Barron: It does. The rate is a hundred and sixty-five a night with breakfast, and the block holds until the twentieth of June.

15
00:01:49.678 --> 00:01:55.416
Niamh Barron: After that they release the rooms, and that weekend is busy, so book before then.

16
00:01:56.112 --> 00:02:00.342
David Barron: Okay, I'll do it today. What nights does the block cover?

17
00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:09.024
Niamh Barron: Thursday the ninth through Sunday the twelfth. So you can do Thursday, Friday, Saturday, out Monday, or any part of that.

18
00:02:09.835 --> 00:02:18.312
David Barron: Cool. I'm looking at flights right now actually. There's an overnight out of Dulles on Wednesday the eighth that lands Thursday morning around seven.

19
00:02:19.157 --> 00:02:22.509
Niamh Barron: Oh, that's good. You'll be wrecked but that's good.

20
00:02:23.635 --> 00:02:32.994
David Barron: Yeah, I'll sleep on the plane, or I won't, either way. And then coming back, Monday the thirteenth, there's one at about eleven in the morning.

21
00:02:34.541 --> 00:02:42.181
Niamh Barron: That works. Monday morning flights are fine from the hotel, it's maybe thirty minutes to the airport if you go early.

22
00:02:42.881 --> 00:02:46.698
David Barron: Okay. Third thing, the RSVP. The card says the fifteenth?

23
00:02:51.813 --> 00:02:58.292
Niamh Barron: The fifteenth of June, yeah. You can just do it on the website, it's quicker than the card.

24
00:02:58.741 --> 00:03:02.851
Niamh Barron: And there's a meal choice: beef, salmon, or the vegetarian risotto.

25
00:03:04.077 --> 00:03:07.932
David Barron: I'll do the salmon. I'll put that in today too.

26
00:03:08.591 --> 00:03:10.891
Niamh Barron: Grand. And it's just you, yeah?

27
00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:13.363
David Barron: Just me, yeah.

28
00:03:14.713 --> 00:03:23.941
Niamh Barron: Okay, I'll tick that off. Oh, and Friday evening, the night before, there's a barbecue at Mum and Dad's for family and anyone who's flown in.

29
00:03:24.009 --> 00:03:26.327
Niamh Barron: Very casual. Starts at six.

30
00:03:27.679 --> 00:03:31.850
David Barron: Oh nice, I'll be there. Do I need to bring anything?

31
00:03:32.493 --> 00:03:37.812
Niamh Barron: Nothing. Just yourself. Maybe a jacket, it gets cold in the garden even in July.

32
00:03:39.181 --> 00:03:43.630
David Barron: Noted. Jacket. What about dress code for Saturday? The invite says "formal".

33
00:03:51.741 --> 00:03:57.009
Niamh Barron: Suit and tie is grand. You don't need a tux. Nobody's wearing a tux.

34
00:03:57.875 --> 00:04:00.842
David Barron: Okay, good, because I don't own one.

35
00:04:01.828 --> 00:04:08.484
Niamh Barron: Ha. Now, the other thing I wanted to ask you. Would you do one of the readings? It's short.

36
00:04:08.969 --> 00:04:13.568
Niamh Barron: It's one of the ones from the booklet, maybe a minute long.

37
00:04:14.388 --> 00:04:22.203
David Barron: Oh. Yeah, of course, I'd be happy to. Do you want me to pick or do you have one in mind?

38
00:04:23.031 --> 00:04:30.948
Niamh Barron: We have one in mind, I'll send it to you. You don't need to memorize it, it'll be printed on the lectern.

39
00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:36.483
David Barron: Okay. Send it whenever. I'll practice it so I don't trip over anything.

40
00:04:37.156 --> 00:04:45.929
Niamh Barron: You'll be fine. Okay, who else is coming over from the States? I'm trying to figure out who arrives when, for the airport runs.

41
00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:55.910
David Barron: So, my parents are coming Wednesday, I think they land Wednesday morning, so a day ahead of me. They said they're booked at the same hotel.

42
00:04:56.111 --> 00:04:57.933
David Barron: And I'm Thursday morning.

43
00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:06.533
Niamh Barron: Okay. I'll put your parents down for Wednesday.

44
00:05:06.915 --> 00:05:14.391
Niamh Barron: Dad offered to pick people up, so I'll tell him Wednesday morning for them and, what time Thursday for you?

45
00:05:15.822 --> 00:05:24.339
David Barron: Lands at seven-ten, so maybe eight by the time I'm through. But honestly I can just get a taxi, he doesn't have to.

46
00:05:25.369 --> 00:05:28.860
Niamh Barron: He'll want to. Just text him when you land.

47
00:05:29.833 --> 00:05:35.412
David Barron: Okay, will do. Is there anything else I should know? Like, gifts, there's a registry?

48
00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:43.672
Niamh Barron: There's a link on the website. But honestly don't worry about it, it's mostly for the older relatives who ask.

49
00:05:44.426 --> 00:05:48.449
David Barron: Okay. I'll take a look. I think that's all my questions.

50
00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:54.316
David Barron: Hotel by the twentieth, RSVP by the fifteenth, salmon, reading, barbecue Friday at six, no car.

51
00:05:55.361 --> 00:05:59.843
Niamh Barron: That's it. You've got it all. I'll send the reading this week.

52
00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:04.971
David Barron: Perfect. It's really good to see you. I'll see you in July.

53
00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:09.251
Niamh Barron: See you in July! Safe travels. Bye!

54
00:06:09.673 --> 00:06:11.219
David Barron: Bye! Stopping the recording.
